    "body": "## motivation\n\nfixes #45225. the qwen3_coder structural tag currently triggers on the text `<tool_call>\\n<function=`, so a literal `<tool_call>` in prose or reasoning can start a constraint, and any other whitespace after the marker never does. xgrammar main (mlc-ai/xgrammar#940) added `token_markers=True`, which matches `<tool_call>` as its dedicated token for `qwen_3_coder`.\n\n## modifications\n\n- `BaseFormatDetector.use_structural_tag_token_markers()` hook, default `False`.\n- `Qwen3CoderDetector` opts in.\n- `get_structural_tag` passes `token_markers=True` only when the detector opts in and the installed `get_model_structural_tag` accepts the argument (signature check). with the pinned xgrammar 0.2.7 / 0.2.8 nothing changes; once the pin moves to a release with #940 the token path turns on.\n\n## tests\n\n`test/registered/unit/function_call/test_qwen3_coder_token_markers.py` (cpu, mocks xgrammar):\n- new api: qwen3_coder gets `token_markers=True`\n- old api: no `token_markers` kwarg (text trigger fallback)\n- detectors without the opt in keep `False`\n- no xgrammar: returns `None`\n\n```\n4 passed\n```\nexisting `test/registered/unit/function_call/` tests that import in a cpu env still pass (105 passed).\n\nnot covered here: an end to end run against xgrammar main with a real qwen3 coder tokenizer, since no release with #940 is out yet.\n\ncc @Ubospica\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39355181007](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39355181007)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39355181064](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39355181064)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39355181046](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39355181046)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
